      "sequence_position": 6,
      "problem": "If $0.35q-0.3=-1$, then $q=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $100$ to get rid of the decimals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.35q-0.3 & =-1 \\\\ 100(0.35q-0.3) & =100(-1) \\\\ 35q-30 & =-100\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the above equation using the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}35q-30 & =-100 \\\\ 35q-30+30 & =-100+30 \\\\ 35q & =-70 \\\\ \\frac{35q}{35} & =\\frac{-70}{35} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{35}q}{\\cancel{35}} & =-\\frac{70}{35} \\\\ q & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
